# ================================================================================================
# samQEq params — Cu ELECTRODE + Zn/ZnCl2/LiCl(aq) NUCLEATION cell (units real, kcal/mol).
# Board task #24 (expanded): the bare-Cu working-electrode leg = the Zn-on-Cu NUCLEATION case.
# Types: 1 Ow, 2 Hw, 3 Zn2+ ion, 4 Cl-, 5 Zn0 (deposited metal, unified w/ ion), 6 Li+, 7 Cu electrode.
#
# Rows 1-6 IDENTICAL to ../p4/p4_multi.param (P0/P1/P4-landed rexsam water + Zn2+/Cl-/Zn0/Li+).
# Row 7 (Cu electrode) is the NEW calibrated entry — the deliverable of this task.
#
# ---- Cu chi/eta CALIBRATION (row 7) --------------------------------------------------------------
# chi_Cu = WORK-FUNCTION anchored.  Convention (newns-anderson-gate memory, "driving channel chi = Phi"):
#   for a metal electrode the samQEq electronegativity chi == the work function Phi (chi = Fermi level
#   position vs vacuum).  Cu polycrystalline Phi = 4.65 eV (facet spread: Cu(110) 4.48 / (100) 4.59 /
#   (111) 4.94; 4.65 = poly/foil, matching the collaborator's bare-Cu WE).
#     chi_Cu = 4.65 eV x 23.0605 = 107.2313 kcal/mol.
#   WHY this fixes P2's unphysical PZC: the electrode fix does chi -> chi - V (fix_qeq_sam_electrode.cpp
#   line 128), so the electrode's Q(V)=0 crossing (PZC) lands at V_deck ~ chi_Cu.  P2 used the generic
#   Rappe atomic chi (3.729 eV) -> PZC ~ +3.5..+4.1 V (deck-absolute), physically meaningless.
#   With chi_Cu = Phi = 4.65 eV the PZC lands at V_deck ~ +4.65 V (absolute-vs-vacuum scale).  The
#   absolute electrode potential of the SHE = 4.44 V (Trasatti), so:
#       E_PZC(vs SHE) = V_deck - 4.44 = 4.65 - 4.44 = +0.21 V  ==  experimental Cu PZC (+0.05..+0.3 V). ✓
#   (residual = the solvent surface-dipole term delta in the Trasatti relation, ~0.1-0.3 eV, uncalibrated.)
#
# eta_Cu = 5.002 eV x 23.0605 = 115.3486 kcal/mol — the Rappe-Goddard atomic hardness (qeq.mst.par
#   "Cu 1 3.729 5.002"), kept as the BARE metallic hardness.  NO soft-eta metal fudge (ion-metal-
#   unification-25): metallic screening emerges from eta_loc; ridge eig conditions the solve regardless
#   (metal-electrode-fq-architectural-wall: there is NO metal-scale wall, always `ridge eig`).
#
# gamma = 0.5 (Angstrom, invariant, matches every other row).  q0 = 0.0 (neutral, INERT metal — Cu is
#   more noble than Zn, does NOT dissolve/deposit; it is the fixed foreign substrate + e- reservoir).
#   ehomo/elumo = 0.0 0.0 (dead columns in the current M2 gate code; not used in populations/rate redox).
#
# Cu is NOT in the demon's REDOX group (only Zn ion/metal = types 3,5 are).  In the FQ solve group are
# water(1,2) + Zn ion/metal(3,5) + Cu(7); Cl(4) and Li(6) stay fixed-formal (P1 sloshing-safe).
# ================================================================================================
